        "E": "3 / 2"
      },
      "answer": "A",
      "explanation": "Same denominator: (3x + 2) / (x + 1).",
      "steps": [
        "1. Fractions with same denominator.",
        "2. Add numerators: 3x + 2.",
        "3. Result: (3x + 2) / (x + 1)."
      ],
      "fastStrategy": "Same denominator: add numerators."
    },
    {
      "id": "mk_re_a_003",
      "question": "Simplify: (2x² - 8) / (x - 2)",
      "choices": {
        "A": "2x + 4",
        "B": "2(x - 2)",
        "C": "2(x + 2)",
        "D": "x + 4",
        "E": "(2x² - 8)/(x - 2)"
      },
      "answer": "C",
      "explanation": "Factor: 2x² - 8 = 2(x² - 4) = 2(x - 2)(x + 2). So (2x² - 8)/(x - 2) = 2(x - 2)(x + 2)/(x - 2) = 2(x + 2).",
      "steps": [
        "1. Factor numerator: 2x² - 8 = 2(x² - 4) = 2(x - 2)(x + 2).",
        "2. Write: (2(x - 2)(x + 2)) / (x - 2).",
        "3. Cancel (x - 2): 2(x + 2)."
      ],
      "fastStrategy": "Factor completely; cancel common factors."
    },
    {
      "id": "mk_re_a_004",
      "question": "What value is excluded from the domain of (x + 3) / (x² - 9)?",
      "choices": {
        "A": "x ≠ 0",
        "B": "x ≠ 3",
        "C": "x ≠ -3",
        "D": "x ≠ 3 and x ≠ -3",
        "E": "No restrictions"
      },
      "answer": "D",
      "explanation": "Denominator cannot be zero: x² - 9 ≠ 0 ⇒ (x - 3)(x + 3) ≠ 0 ⇒ x ≠ 3 and x ≠ -3.",
      "steps": [
        "1. Set denominator to zero: x² - 9 = 0.",
        "2. Factor: (x - 3)(x + 3) = 0.",
        "3. Solve: x = 3 or x = -3.",
        "4. Excluded values: x ≠ 3 and x ≠ -3."
      ],
      "fastStrategy": "Domain: denominator ≠ 0."
    }
  ]
